The linked OpenAI Developers page explains that Codex can now operate desktop apps while working, enhancing its functionality and accessibility.

You don't need the full Codex app on your remote server. Just install the CLI and run: codex remote-control. Your phone's ChatGPT app will pick it up as a remote server, showing a terminal icon instead of the computer icon from the full app. It's the same experience with way less setup.

The future is coding from bed; it's going to heal my back pain at least.

